        <mxCell id="note_scope" value="&lt;b&gt;What crosses&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The column-listed publications decide what PostgreSQL emits, and each mirror's column exclusions decide what PeerDB writes, so a non-allowlisted column never reaches ClickHouse, the Avro staging or PeerDB's logs (gate G6.4). peerdb-bootstrap admits one source at a time: order, then checkout, then payment, each after its heartbeat and every table's row count arrive. Beside each raw table PeerDB keeps a _peerdb_raw_&amp;lt;mirror&amp;gt; staging table; the _live views run as definer analytics_view_owner, so analytics_reader needs no grant on the raw tables." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1300" width="890" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_boot" value="&lt;b&gt;Who creates the path&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nothing is created by hand. In the cdc-local wave, peerdb-bootstrap calls flow-api to upsert the peers and create the three mirrors, and analytics-views creates the ten *_live views once the raw tables exist. product-db-cdc-bootstrap, in the databases wave (Job, then a CronJob every 10 min), creates the heartbeat tables, schedules the pg_cron jobs and grants peerdb_&amp;lt;db&amp;gt; SELECT on exactly the tables its publication carries." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1392" width="890" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_tls" value="&lt;b&gt;Credentials and TLS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every PostgreSQL hop verifies the homelab-ca certificate: PeerDB to the CDC pooler, the pooler to the primary, and PeerDB to its catalog. ClickHouse and RustFS are plaintext inside the cluster: ClickHouse TLS is ADR-069 obligation T1, and RustFS's shared key is the open part of ADR-066's isolation obligation (#1315). PeerDB logs in to each database as peerdb_&amp;lt;db&amp;gt; and to ClickHouse (native :9000) as analytics_ingest; analytics-service reads only the views, as analytics_reader. The flow-snapshot-worker holds the slot's exported snapshot while flow-worker copies the tables from it; flow-worker also writes mirror state to the catalog." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1474" width="890" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" value="Legend" style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=12;verticalAlign=top;html=1;container=1;collapsible=0;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#334155;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1584" width="890" height="88" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
